cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use processbehavior in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "processbehavior: Process Behavior Charts and Variance Analysis for Python"
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation of Thomas A. Bishop's Variance Analysis System (VAS):
  three-state design-state lineage detection (planned / observed / analytical),
  process behavior charts, R1-R6 residual variance decomposition, capability
  indices, and Taguchi loss functions. Analytical outputs are validated
  assertion-by-assertion against Bishop's published Minitab reference results.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nicholas
    given-names: Chris
    email: chris.nicholas@gmail.com
  - family-names: Bishop
    given-names: Thomas
    name-suffix: A.
repository-code: "https://github.com/cnicholas/processbehavior"
url: "https://cnicholas.github.io/processbehavior/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.1
keywords:
  - statistical process control
  - process behavior charts
  - variance analysis
  - control charts
  - quality control
  - shewhart
  - design of experiments

references:
  - type: book
    title: "The Scientific Basis for Modern Analytic Practice"
    abstract: >-
      The methodological foundation for the Variance Analysis System this
      package implements: applied-research foundations, scientific methodology,
      Shewhart's inductive analytic approach and process behavior charts,
      operational definitions and research protocols, and case studies.
    authors:
      - family-names: Bishop
        given-names: Thomas
    year: 2021
    month: 4
    publisher:
      name: "Lulu Press, Inc."
    url: "https://www.lulu.com/shop/thomas-bishop/the-scientific-basis-for-modern-analytic-practice/paperback/product-k7e8dk.html"
